{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.7b9e7a5ec6","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"pron-o-8","passage":"<p>The newspaper announced that ______ new schedule had been approved.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["it's","its","their","they're"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the newspaper,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.7785282ee4","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"pron-o-9","passage":"<p>The zoo announced that ______ new schedule had been approved.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["their","its","they're","it's"],"answer":"B","explanation":"A pronoun must agree with the noun it refers to. Here that noun is “the zoo,” which is singular. The singular possessive pronoun is “its” (“it's” means “it is”)."},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.6efeac5080","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"tense-9","passage":"<p>Since 2015, the researcher ______ two new species of beetle.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["has discovered","will discover","had discovered","discovered"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “Since 2015,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has discovered.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.2.d0dc419749","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"tense-13","passage":"<p>So far this year, the university ______ hundreds of scholarships.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["awarded","had awarded","has awarded","will award"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The verb tense must fit the time frame of the sentence, which is set by “So far this year,” a period that continues up to the present, so the present perfect (“has” plus the past participle) is needed. The correct choice is “has awarded.”"}
